## 2026-10-01 — Item physics + spacing for item rings
- graph.ts ringPhysics(): events/projects/actions around a group are now a small force simulation (radial pull to their ring, collision, gentle repulsion, a spring to their home spot). They spill out of the group, jostle into place, can be dragged (the others make room) and spring back on release; clicking still opens the card (drag threshold 4px). Used for the zoomed-in group view and the always-on zoomed-in item bubbles.
- Spacing: each group's collision radius now covers its ring of items when "Always on" is selected (itemExtent + 18px), so neighbouring groups' items don't overlap; recalculated when the item settings change. In the zoomed-in group view, other groups (and their items) are pushed clear of the focus ring.
- Tested in Playwright: focus bubbles move and settle with 0 overlaps; dragging one 211px moves others and it returns to 0px from home after release; card still opens on click; always-on view spreads groups; no page errors.
- Uncertainty: with "Always on", the whole network spreads out more (by design); the dot-level view uses the zoomed-in ring size for spacing so the layout doesn't jump when you zoom.

