## 2026-10-02 — Seamless zoom, planets with moons, full names, coalition About + details, new loading screen
- Zoom no longer reshuffles the map. Item orbits and group spacing are now the same at every zoom: no more planet doubling or collide change at the detail threshold. Dots turn into icons in the same places at the same size, and icons keep a steady on-screen size (CSS --is), so planets grow around them as you zoom. Item names appear beside the icons from 2.8× zoom, as light unboxed text reading away from the planet: full name plus one meta line. Measured: 0.0 px node movement while zooming from 1× to 4×.
- Past 100% zoom, group names and lines keep their on-screen size (CSS --ns, non-scaling strokes), so they no longer balloon over neighbours.
