## 2026-10-03 — Topics page: "Command room" view (scheduled run)
- Why: Nathan's saved choice from the command-room brainstorm (claude.ai project doc "Topics view: command room idea"): show where the groups' problem-solving energy flows, Galcon / WarGames style but about repair, grand but calm.
- Based on development_branch (#35 and #37 are merged). Open PRs checked first: only #40 (logos), which doesn't touch the Topics page.
- New src/commandroom.ts, shown by a "Bubbles | Command room" switch in the Topics header (remembered in localStorage). topics.ts now exports TopicsFile, hands the command room its weight function, cap and colours, and calls update() when a slider moves.
- Energy: each record's weight is the same slider weight the bubbles use. A stream is one group → one problem; its value is the sum of its records' weights, capped by "Cap per group". A record counts fully for each topic it's tagged with (same as the bubbles), not split between them.
- Importance: new "Problem importance" sliders (one per parent topic, "Not important → Important", default 0.5; Broad climate 0.2) in the side panel, open in the command room. Coverage = the problem's share of all energy ÷ its share of all importance (Broad climate left out of both). Child topics: the parent's coverage × the child's energy ÷ the mean of its siblings'. Glow = min(1, coverage/1.25)^0.75.
- Layouts: (a) groups in the middle, placed toward the problems they feed (focused groups near the rim, generalists in the centre, collision-relaxed), problems on a ring; (b) groups in a column on the left (staggered when crowded, ordered by where their energy goes), problems on the right.
- Styles: "Comets + shields" (glowing particles with short fading tails on curved arcs; the problem's shield, coverage arc and blurred glow follow coverage) and "Watershed" (rivulets from each group join one river per problem; the delta goes from cracked dry ground to a green-blue wetland with reeds as coverage rises).
- Zoomed out: one stream per group → parent topic. Clicking a parent, "Split all", or zooming past 1.7× splits parents into child topics. Clicking a split group's arc/label folds it back; background click clears the selection, then folds.
- Zoom moves nodes rather than scaling them (labels stay readable); canvas strokes and particles are kept at screen size.
- Hover a stream: highlight + "group → problem", energy and its top 3 items. Click a group: only its streams + its items by problem, and a map link. Click a problem: who feeds it (bars, each with map ↗) and its items with item links and group → map links.
- Playback (Sep 2026 → May 2027, the span of dated events; about 9 days a second): undated projects/actions/missions are always on; one-off events appear on their date (ripple) and fade over a few weeks; repeating events stay on and pulse weekly. In the whole-year view, problems with repeating events pulse gently every 7–11 s.
- Calm: canvas particles with a fixed budget (one per live stream plus the rest of ≤650 comets / ≤850 water glints shared by weight; about 490 / 710 on a 1440×900 screen), speeds of 12–38 px/s, low opacity, additive blending; the static stream layer is cached in an offscreen canvas. prefers-reduced-motion: no animation loop, static dotted flows, playback steps every 0.4 s.
- "Where is help needed?": dims everything except problems with importance ≥ 0.5 and coverage < 0.7, and lists them (click to open). With default sliders on MA: Food & farming, Democracy, Resilience, Other movements (0.3×), Education, Jobs (0.6×).
- Kept the draft note and the dimmed, dashed "Broad climate". Ring and labels leave room for the site's round + button.
- Playwright (vite preview, 1440×900, headless Chromium without a GPU): both layouts × both styles, hover, click problem/group, the map link, help, playback + scrub, zoom split (75 problems), Split all, slider update, importance slider (food 0.5→1 dims its core 0.30→0.22), Reset, Bubbles ↔ Command room, reduced motion (0 animation frames), phone width. Average drawing work 0.9–2.2 ms per frame, frame interval ≈16.7 ms. 0 page errors.
  - Console errors that are not from this PR: "translate(NaN,NaN) scale(NaN)" from graph.ts after visiting the Map tab and leaving it before it settles (already logged on 2026-10-03), and one 404 during page load that didn't reproduce.

